<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antoine-Martin Chaumont de La Galaizière</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1697">1697</a>–<a href="/years/1783">1783</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antoine-Martin Chaumont de La Galaizière was a French administrator who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> as chancellor for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski">Stanisław Leszczyński</a> from 1737 to 1766. Under the secret <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/declaration-of-meudon">Declaration of Meudon</a> of 1736 Stanisław left real power to him, and he prepared the duchy's absorption into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, completed on Stanisław's death in 1766, through French taxes, forced labour and administration.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antoine-martin-chaumont-de-la-galaiziere.jpg" alt="Antoine-Martin Chaumont de La Galaizière" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François-André Vincent · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fran%C3%A7ois-Andr%C3%A9_Vincent_-_La_Galaizi%C3%A8re_est_cr%C3%A9%C3%A9_chancelier_par_Stanislas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
